  "reveal": {
    "brief_voiced": "The killer was Wat Frew. The touch faltered twice. Fides tripped about the first minute of the touch; the green hand's own trip — a new hand's stumble convicts nobody, and the tower thinks no worse of it. But Patientia hung late where the method wanted her elsewhere, and no custom excuses it; that rope was in Wat Frew's keeping, and the hands that should have held it were free about the third minute of the touch. Fifi Swain did not survive the office.\n\nAs to the why of it: Of Wat Frew, the playbill says: Captain Wat Frew — a sea-captain of elastic accounts; owed money by half the company. Of Fifi Swain: Fenella \"Fifi\" Swain — a lady's-maid, twin to Zane; hears more than a servant ought.\n\nThe tower proved every pair of hands but one.",
